{#- Observed change after escalation (Calculation Methodology 7). Two runs in
    one market, same grid and same repeats, at one persona. Never a single
    figure "improved by X%". -#}
{%- for block in claim.cleansing %}
<div class="panel"><table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Repeat rate before and after the disclosure in {{ block.before.country | countryName }}, persona {{ block.persona }} only, never averaged across personas</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">{{ 'col.chatbot' | t }}</th>
    <th scope="col" class="num">Before (<time datetime="{{ block.before.collected_at | isoDate }}">{{ block.before.collected_at | shortDate }}</time>)</th>
    <th scope="col" class="num">After (<time datetime="{{ block.after.collected_at | isoDate }}">{{ block.after.collected_at | shortDate }}</time>)</th>
    <th scope="col">{{ 'col.change' | t }}</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for row in block.rows %}
    <tr data-persona="{{ block.persona }}">
      <th scope="row" style="font-weight:400">{{ row.chatbot | botName }}</th>
      <td class="num"><span class="cellstat{% if row.before.low_n %} lown{% endif %}">{{ row.before.rate | rate }}<small>{{ row.before.ci | ciLabel }} &middot; n={{ row.before.n }}</small></span></td>
      <td class="num"><span class="cellstat{% if row.after.low_n %} lown{% endif %}">{{ row.after.rate | rate }}<small>{{ row.after.ci | ciLabel }} &middot; n={{ row.after.n }}</small></span></td>
      <td class="rmeta" style="color:var({{ '--ok' if row.change.significant and row.change.delta < 0 else '--dim' }})">
        {{ row.change.delta | pp }}
        <small style="display:block;color:var(--dimmer)">{{ "significant" if row.change.significant else "not significant" }}</small></td>
    </tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>
<p class="note">Measured under persona {{ block.persona }} &middot; {{ block.persona | personaLabel }}, in
  {{ block.before.country | countryName }} only. A change is called real only when the two intervals do not
  overlap. There is no control group: a change here cannot be separated from a model update in the same
  window, so this is the change observed after the disclosure, not the effect of it. Model versions are
  recorded on both sides.</p>
{%- endfor %}
